{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.WStdSuperExponential","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.WStdSuperExponential","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SkewBranchingTwoOne","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingGevreyHalf","lean:module:QOU.Mass.LevelSelectionLogarithmic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.no_superlinear_selection_wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.no_superlinear_selection_wStd","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L216-L220","doc":"**Super-linear selection — bond-count `A(A−1)/2` included — likewise.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.no_linear_selection_wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.no_linear_selection_wStd","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L211-L214","doc":"**Linear level-selection is excluded, unconditionally, for the real `w_std`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.towerGeometricLowerBound_wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.towerGeometricLowerBound_wStd","kind":"instance","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L197-L203","doc":"**The class is inhabited at `k₀ = 3`** — the first threshold the previous result allows,\nand exactly where `w_std` stops vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.not_towerGeometricLowerBound_wStd_of_lt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.not_towerGeometricLowerBound_wStd_of_lt_three","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L180-L195","doc":"**No threshold below 3 is satisfiable, for any `r` and `c`.**\n\nAt `k = k₀ < 3` the class's own field reads `c · r^{k₀} ≤ w_std(k₀) = 0`, against `c_pos` and\n`r > 0`. A structural exclusion with a named invariant (the `fDimSkew` containment guard), not\na scope-limited negative: no choice of constants repairs it, which is why the class carries a\nthreshold rather than better constants.\n\nIn particular the class's previous `∀ k` form — the `k₀ = 0` case here — was **false**, so\nevery result conditional on it was conditional on a falsehood. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_geometric_from_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_geometric_from_three","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L160-L176","doc":"**The geometric bound: `(1/30)·(√2)^k ≤ w_std(k)` for `k ≥ 3`.**\n\nThis is exactly `TowerGeometricLowerBound.lower_bound` with `r = √2 > 1` and `c = 1/30 > 0`,\nrestricted to `k ≥ 3` — which is all that is possible, since `w_std` vanishes below it, and all\nthat `no_linear_selection` / `no_superlinear_selection` consume, since both pick their `A` from\nan `atTop` filter. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:tower-geometric-lower-bound","label":"prop:tower-geometric-lower-bound","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tower-geometric-lower-bound.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_sq_ge_two_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_sq_ge_two_pow","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L141-L158","doc":"**`2^k/900 ≤ w_std(k)²` for `k ≥ 3`** — `wStd_sq_lower` with `k!` bounded below via\n`nine_four_pow_le_hundred_factorial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.nine_four_pow_le_hundred_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.nine_four_pow_le_hundred_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L124-L139","doc":"`9·4^k ≤ 100·k!` for `k ≥ 3` — the integer step behind the geometric bound.\n\nTight at the base: `9·4³ = 576` against `100·3! = 600`.  The weaker constant is what buys the\nlow threshold; the sharper `4^k ≤ k!` is first true only at `k = 9` (it fails at `k = 8`,\n`65536 > 40320`), which is where an earlier version of this file had to start. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_sq_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_sq_lower","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L99-L120","doc":"**`k!/(81·2^k) ≤ w_std(k)²`, unconditionally, for `k ≥ 3`.**\n\n`BindingGevreyHalf.wstd_superexp_sq` supplies the inequality from two hypotheses its own\ndocstring calls \"the open combinatorial core\". Both are now theorems: (A) is\n`branching_two_one_holds`, (C) is `skew_le_straight` composed with\n`sum_dimSYT_eq_involution`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_eq_zero_of_lt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_eq_zero_of_lt_three","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L88-L95","doc":"**`w_std(k) = 0` for `k < 3`** — every term carries a `fDimSkew` that the containment\nguard sends to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.fDimSkew_mu21_eq_zero_of_card_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.fDimSkew_mu21_eq_zero_of_card_lt","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L83-L86","doc":"A diagram with fewer than three cells cannot contain `(2,1)`, so its skew count is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L77-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WStd.wStd","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WStdSuperExponential.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**The Plancherel-weighted branched tower weight**\n`w_std(k) = (∑_{λ ⊢ k} (f^λ)² · f^{λ/(2,1)}) / k!`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}